{
  "case_id": "2007-06-856",
  "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sections 502(a)(2) and 409 of ERISA permit restoration of \"any losses to the plan.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What are the code numbers of those? I really get confused with you people who work with ERISA all the time -- can refer, you know Section 3 of ERISA. I use the code. What -- what code sections are you talking about?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, the statute plainly states that \"any losses to the plan\" may be recovered if they were caused by fiduciary breach. Our position on the (a)(2) question is straightforward. The plain meaning of \"any losses to the plan\" includes any diminution in value of defined contribution plan assets, regardless of the number of participants ultimately affected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is in the record; it was attached to the complaint that was filed by Mr. LaRue in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought your own argument was that (a)(3) is the catchall. So if (a)(2), which is described as very precise, if that's applicable, you would not get to (a)(3). You would be asking us at this point to assume that somehow the (a)(2) case folds, and then we flip over into (a)(3)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0001-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "losses are diminution in trust assets or failure of trust assets to appreciate. But there are individual pecuniary losses that were historically remediable under surcharge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ERISA authorizes a participant in a defined contribution plan to sue to recover losses to the plan caused by a fiduciary breach even if the losses are attributable to the participant's individual plan account."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Unlike Section (a)(2), which refers you to 1109, does not say who gets sued."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "clarify what the government's position is on this (a)(1)(B) argument? Are you saying it is available, but (a)(2) is available?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, that is an oddity but what do you say to Mr. Roberts' argument that the only recovery under (a)(1)(B) is against the plan, and the plan doesn't have the money in the account so that if there is going to be any relief it's got to come from the fiduciary and that gets you into (2)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it entirely clear that the plan itself does not have any money to pay this off unless it takes the money from other individual accounts? I thought one of the briefs said that -- that some plans have independent funds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gies",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GIES: Well, we think that (a)(2), properly read, does not permit an individual claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gies",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GIES: We think relief in that situation, including recovery of the diamonds and any profits associated with it, would be available under (a)(3)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Well, I'm sorry. I'm not interested in that question. I'm interested in my question. Why isn't it available under (a)(2)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Then what is your theory on how we determine whether a loss to the plan from an individual account suffices as a loss to the plan for purposes of pleading?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Let's take, because this case was tossed out on the pleadings, the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gies",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e84af8b76a3f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GIES: We think that Congress did not want those kinds of claims to be brought under (a)(2) precisely for that kind of reason. There would be no end to the kind of arguments about damages. And those kind of cases impose costs that will ultimately be borne by the plans, which is inconsistent with the congressional purpose in ERISA to encourage plan formation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2007-06-856",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "e84af8b76a3f99ec010531d8476a3f3114cfeb26f959979e412335019fdd6bdc",
